{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1793264532","published":"2026-10-29T09:02:31Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:30.532788919Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-12818","CVE-2026-2004","CVE-2026-2005","CVE-2026-2006"],"summary":"Fix of 16 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: integer overflows leading to out-of-bounds writes in\n     libpq\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-12818.patch: guard size and length\n       computations against int and size_t overflow in\n       src/interfaces/libpq/fe-connect.c, src/interfaces/libpq/fe-exec.c,\n       src/interfaces/libpq/fe-print.c, src/interfaces/libpq/fe-protocol3.c\n       and src/interfaces/libpq/libpq-int.h.\n     - CVE-2025-12818\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds reads via missing validation of\n     multibyte character length\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-2006.patch: add bounds-checked pg_mblen_cstr(),\n       pg_mblen_range(), pg_mblen_with_len() and pg_mblen_unbounded() and use\n       them in place of pg_mblen() across the backend and contrib modules,\n       fix EUC_CN maximum length and mb2wchar functions on short input in\n       src/backend/utils/mb/wchar.c, and require PGP-decrypted text to pass\n       encoding validation in contrib/pgcrypto/pgp-pgsql.c, with tests.\n     - CVE-2026-2006\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: arbitrary code execution via non-built-in selectivity\n     estimators\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-2004.patch: require superuser to install a\n       non-built-in selectivity estimator in\n       src/backend/commands/operatorcmds.c, and check input types in\n       src/backend/tsearch/ts_selfuncs.c and\n       src/backend/utils/adt/network_selfuncs.c.\n     - CVE-2026-2004\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer overflow in pgcrypto pgp_pub_decrypt_bytea()\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-2005.patch: reject oversized session keys in\n       contrib/pgcrypto/pgp-pubdec.c, add PXE_PGP_KEY_TOO_BIG to\n       contrib/pgcrypto/px.h and contrib/pgcrypto/px.c, with tests.\n     - CVE-2026-2005","affected":[{"package":